│   │   ├── fleet/            # Agones fleet lifecycle
│   │   ├── meta/             # Meta persistence and RPCs
│   │   ├── net/              # WebSocket gateway (ws://localhost:2567)
│   │   ├── physics/          # rapier2d physics integration
│   │   └── main.rs           # Server entry point
│   └── tests/                # Rust integration tests
├── game-client/              # Godot 4.7 C# NativeAOT 3D client
│   ├── src/                  # C# gameplay, world, camera, entity views
│   └── assets/               # Baked res:// assets and manifests
├── contracts/                # Shared TypeScript types and content contracts
├── client/react-client/      # React web client (debug/web view)
├── content/                  # Authoritative world, story, map, character, studio data
├── atelier/                  # Asset/story/map build tools and review panels
├── scripts/                  # Gate scripts (fastcheck.sh, precheck.sh, check_content.mjs)
└── docs/                     # Authoritative specs (unit-contract.md, *.spec.md)
```

## Architecture Principles

### Server-Side (`server-rs/`)
- **Server-authoritative, always** — physics (`rapier2d`), movement, combat, HP, and meta state run on `server-rs/`.
- **Simulated time as input** — gate per-tick work on `SimClock` (`server-rs/src/core/clock.rs`), never `Instant::now()`.
- **Unit contract (`docs/unit-contract.md`)** — `1 game unit = 1 metre`, `coord_scale = 1.0`. Never mask a scale bug by changing `coord_scale` alone.

### Client-Side (`game-client/` & `client/react-client/`)
- **Input intents only** — clients send movement vectors and discrete actions, never authoritative positions or damage.
- **Godot 4.7 C# (`game-client/`)** — primary 3D runtime; forward axis `-Z`, up `+Y`, `1 unit = 1 metre`, slim-adventurer character band `0.90–1.20 m` (`1.05 m` reference).
- **Web client (`client/react-client/`)** — lightweight browser client consuming `@atlas/contracts`.

## Development & Verification Commands

```bash
# Mid-iteration fast check (<15s)
./scripts/fastcheck.sh

# Full Gate 1 pre-ship check
./scripts/precheck.sh --no-install

# Rust server
cd server-rs && cargo fmt --check && cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo test

# Contracts (pnpm workspace at repo root)
cd contracts && pnpm run build && pnpm test && npx tsc --noEmit

# Web client
cd client/react-client && CI=true npx react-scripts test --watchAll=false

# Content & script gates
node scripts/check_content.mjs
node --test scripts/tests/*.test.mjs
```

## Code Quality & Conventions
- **Modularity** — keep modules focused and single-responsibility; avoid monolithic dumps (`scripts/lint_file_size.py` enforces ceilings on Python observatory tooling).
- **Rust** — `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` must pass cleanly.
- **TypeScript** — strict mode, no unjustified `any`, Prettier + ESLint clean.
- **C# (`game-client/`)** — verify with `./scripts/godot-verify.sh` and headless `/Users/pasitnusso/.local/bin/godot-bg`.
- **Branching & Commits** — trunk-based (`feature/`, `fix/`, `docs/`), squash-merge only, conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`). Release work routes through `ps-release-workflow` (`.release.json`).
